R"VG(
# song2.vg (H-04's second pass): the song's register (song.vg's refrains): the land and the sky, the works, the coming and the leaving,
# and the everyday (a fair, a fire, a storm, a champion, a trial, a disaster of the works...), each in three lines and a refrain.

# ---- the land and the sky -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

song.flood
  {ann.sg.fl.a}\n{ann.sg.fl.b}\n{ann.sg.fl.c}\n{song.refrain}
ann.sg.fl.a
  The river rose at {$e.place}, the river rose over the {crop},
  ($e.flood=sea) The sea came in at {$e.place} and did not knock,
  It rained on {mountain} and it rained on us, and the water came down through the {tree},
  The water came over the {crop} in {$e.season},
ann.sg.fl.b
  it took the houses and it took the {herd},
  we stood on the {roofs} and counted the ones on the other roofs,
  it took the {vessel} and the seed and the cradles,
  the {tree} stood in it up to their arms,
ann.sg.fl.c
  and when it went down it left the {tree} standing in mud,
  and the mud it left was good for the {crop}, so they say,
  ($e.value>0) and {#$e.value:about} went down the river and did not come back,
  and we built again higher up, of {material}, and it found us there too,

song.famine
  {ann.sg.fam.a}\n{ann.sg.fam.b}\n{ann.sg.fam.c}\n{song.refrain}
ann.sg.fam.a
  There was no {crop} in {$e.season}, there was no {crop},
  The {vessel} were empty and the {herd} were bones,
  Hungry, hungry, from the {crop} fields all the way to {mountain},
ann.sg.fam.b
  we ate the seed and then we ate the {tree.n} bark,
  we boiled the {herd} hides and we chewed the straps,
  the children stopped crying for {food}, and that was worse,
  we dug for roots with {tool} in the frozen ground,
ann.sg.fam.c
  ($e.value>0) {#$e.value:about} went hungry to {deadplace},
  and the old ones went out past {town.edge} and did not come back,
  and when the {crop} came again we wept into it,

song.quake
  {ann.sg.qk.a}\n{ann.sg.qk.b}\n{ann.sg.qk.c}\n{song.refrain}
ann.sg.qk.a
  The ground at {$e.place} turned over in its sleep,
  The earth at {$e.place} shook like a wet {beast},
  In {$e.season} the ground stood up at {$e.place},
ann.sg.qk.b
  and the {walls.of} walls came down on the ones inside,
  and the {roofs} fell in on the sleepers,
  and {holyplace} cracked from the top to the floor,
ann.sg.qk.c
  and we dug with our hands and {tool} until {skyone} rose,
  and we slept with the {herd} in the fields for a month after,
  and {watersrc} ran muddy and then ran clear,

song.eruption
  {mountain} woke up angry, {mountain} woke up red,\n{ann.sg.er.b}\n{song.refrain}
  The top of {mountain} came off in {$e.season},\n{ann.sg.er.b}\n{song.refrain}
ann.sg.er.b
  and the ash came down on {$e.place} like snow that does not melt,
  and the {herd} lay down in the grey and did not get up,
  and the day went dark over the {crop} and stayed dark for a week,

song.impact
  A stone came down from the sky at {$e.place},\n{ann.sg.imp.b}\n{song.refrain}
  A star fell, and it fell on {$e.place},\n{ann.sg.imp.b}\n{song.refrain}
ann.sg.imp.b
  and the sky went dark and the {crop} did not come up,
  and the light of it was seen from {$seat},
  and where {$e.place} stood there is a pond,

song.winter
  {ann.sg.win.a}\n{ann.sg.win.b}\n{song.refrain}
ann.sg.win.a
  The winter came and the winter stayed,
  The snow came down on the {roofs} and did not lift,
  {season.next} never came that year, or the next,
ann.sg.win.b
  the {crop} lay under the snow until it rotted,
  we burned the {fuel} and then the fences and then the {vessel},
  the {herd} stood in the drifts and froze standing,

song.drought
  {ann.sg.dr.a}\n{ann.sg.dr.b}\n{song.refrain}
ann.sg.dr.a
  No rain, no rain, the {watersrc.n} gave sand,
  The sky was brass from {festival} to {festival},
  Dry, dry, the {crop} came up and lay down,
ann.sg.dr.b
  the {herd} lay down in the dry beds of the streams,
  and we carried water in {vessel} from far away,
  and the priests went up to {holyplace} every day with {offering}, for nothing,

song.omen
  ($e.omen=comet) The hairy star came back as the old ones said,\n{ann.sg.om.b}\n{song.refrain}
  ($e.omen=eclipse) The sun went out at noon at {$e.place},\n{ann.sg.om.b}\n{song.refrain}
  ($e.omen!=comet $e.omen!=eclipse) There was a sign in the sky over {$e.place},\n{ann.sg.om.b}\n{song.refrain}
ann.sg.om.b
  and we stood in the {crop} and watched it pass,
  and the priests said this and the {ann.craftfolk} said that,
  and the {herd} would not settle all night,
  and the children were brought out of {ann.house1} to see it,

# ---- the works and the places -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

song.founding
  {ann.sg.fd.a}\n{ann.sg.fd.b}\n{ann.sg.fd.c}\n{song.refrain}
ann.sg.fd.a
  (!has:$e.a) Somebody came to {$e.place} when there was nothing there,
  (has:$e.a) {$e.a:name} came to {$e.place} when there was nothing there,
  When {$e.place} was a field and a {watersrc.n},
  They walked to {$e.place} with the fire in {vessel.one},
ann.sg.fd.b
  only the {tree} and the water and the wind,
  only the {bird} and the long grass and the {game},
  and they built {ann.house1} and were cold in it,
ann.sg.fd.c
  and set down {vessel.one} and said: here, and it was here,
  and the {herd} were the first to stay,
  and now it is {$e.place}, with {ann.houses}, and nobody remembers it was not,

song.built
  {ann.sg.bt.a}\n{ann.sg.bt.b}\n{ann.sg.bt.c}\n{song.refrain}
ann.sg.bt.a
  They carried the stone for {$e.work} {#$e.value|year},
  They raised {$e.work} at {$e.place} with their hands,
  Who built {$e.work}? The ones with sore backs did,
ann.sg.bt.b
  and their hands were raw from the {material} and their backs were bent,
  and the {ann.craft.or.work} stopped while it went up,
  and {motif.over} were cut over the door by somebody's son,
ann.sg.bt.c
  and now it stands at {$e.place} and the {herd} graze round it,
  and the {bird} nest in it, and that is right,
  and we walk past it with the {vessel} every day and do not look up,
ann.craft.or.work
  {craft}
  work in the fields

song.exodus
  {ann.sg.ex.a}\n{ann.sg.ex.b}\n{song.refrain}
ann.sg.ex.a
  They left {$e.place} with the carts and the {herd},
  We left {$e.place} in {$e.season}, with what we could carry,
  The roads out of {$e.place} were full for {#n|day},
ann.sg.ex.b
  and they did not look back at the {ann.houses}, and we did not wave,
  and the {colour.holy} cloth went with them, and the songs,
  and the doors stood open behind them for the wind and the {bird},

song.end
  (!has:$e.a) The last of us was at {$e.place}, alone,\n{ann.sg.end.b}\n{song.refrain}
  (has:$e.a) {$e.a:name} was the last, at {$e.place}, alone,\n{ann.sg.end.b}\n{song.refrain}
  (has:$e.a) At {$e.place} the last fire was kept by {$e.a:name},\n{ann.sg.end.b}\n{song.refrain}
ann.sg.end.b
  and there was nobody to sing it, so we sing it now, to {instrument},
  and the {herd} came to the door and nobody came out,
  and {skyone} went over and went over, and nobody counted,

song.coming
  We came into the land {song.whence},\n{ann.sg.cm.b}\n{song.refrain}
  Our mothers' mothers came {song.whence},\n{ann.sg.cm.b}\n{song.refrain}
ann.sg.cm.b
  we came with the {herd} and the fire in {vessel.one},
  and the land was empty and the {crop} grew wild,
  and the {game} did not know to run from us yet,
song.whence
  ($e.whence=mountain) over {mountain}
  ($e.whence=sea) over {sea}
  ($e.whence=north) out of the north
  ($e.whence=south) out of the south
  ($e.whence=east|$e.whence=west) from where the sun goes
  ($e.whence=river) down {river}
  ($e.whence=dry) across the dry country

song.stones
  We raised the stones where {city} would be,\n{#number} stones for the {#number} winds,\n{ann.sg.st.c}\n{song.refrain}
ann.sg.st.c
  and they stand there still among the {tree}, and we are still here,
  and we dance round them at {festival} with {feast.custom}, and nobody knows why,

song.contact
  {ann.sg.ct.a}\n{ann.sg.ct.b}\n{song.refrain}
ann.sg.ct.a
  The {other} came to {$e.place}, tall and strange,
  (has:$e.season) We met the {other} at {$e.place} in {$e.season},
  We met the {other} at {$e.place}, by the water,
ann.sg.ct.b
  and they held out their hands, and we held out {vessel} of {crop},
  and they would not eat our {food}, and we laughed,
  and their speech was like {watersrc} running, and we did not know it,

song.none
  Sing for {river}, it gives the water,\nsing for the {herd}, they give the milk,\nsing for {skyone}, who keeps the time,\n{song.refrain}
  Sing for the {crop}, it fills the {vessel},\nsing for the {tree}, they give the shade,\nsing for {mountain}, it keeps the wind off,\n{song.refrain}

# ---- the everyday -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

song.fair
  {ann.sg.fair.a}\n{ann.sg.fair.b}\n{song.refrain}
ann.sg.fair.a
  ($e.what=gathering) We went down to {$e.place} where the bands all meet,
  ($e.what!=gathering) Oh the fair at {$e.place}, the fair in {$e.season},
  I went to {$e.place} with {vessel} of {crop} and came home with a song,
ann.sg.fair.b
  with a {beast} on a string and a song in my mouth,
  and I sold the {herd} and I bought a {garment.n},
  and I danced the {~dance} with someone whose name I forgot,

song.fire
  {ann.sg.fire.a}\n{ann.sg.fire.b}\n{song.refrain}
ann.sg.fire.a
  Fire in {$e.place}, fire in the night,
  The {roofs} of {$e.place} went up like straw,
  In {$e.season} the fire came down the street,
ann.sg.fire.b
  and we stood in a line with the {vessel} and it laughed at us,
  ($e.value>0) and {#$e.value|house} were ash by the morning,
  and the wind was its friend, and the wind was not ours, and the {herd} ran,

song.storm
  {ann.sg.stm.a}\n{ann.sg.stm.b}\n{song.refrain}
ann.sg.stm.a
  ($e.what=sea) The sea got up and walked in {$e.season},
  ($e.what=snow) The snow came down for {#n|day},
  ($e.what=dust) The dust came out of the dry country like a wall,
  ($e.what=hail) The hail came down like stones from a sling,
  The wind came over {mountain} and it did not stop,
ann.sg.stm.b
  and it took the roofs and it took the {crop},
  and the {herd} were found three valleys away,
  and we sat in the dark under the {roofs} and held the children,

song.pest
  {ann.sg.pst.a}\n{ann.sg.pst.b}\n{song.refrain}
ann.sg.pst.a
  ($e.what=locusts) The locusts came down like a cloud on the fields,
  ($e.what=murrain) The {herd} lay down and did not get up,
  ($e.what=wolves) The wolves came down off {mountain} in the hungry time,
  The {crop} went black in the fields round {$e.place},
ann.sg.pst.b
  and what they left the {bird} took,
  and we cursed it, {exclaim}, and it made no difference,

song.wonder
  {ann.sg.wnd.a}\n{ann.sg.wnd.b}\n{song.refrain}
ann.sg.wnd.a
  ($e.what=calf) A calf with two heads was born at {$e.place},
  ($e.what=fish) They pulled a fish from the water at {$e.place} as long as a boat,
  ($e.what=beast) A white {game.one} came down to {$e.place} and looked at us,
  ($e.what=tree) The {tree.n} at {$e.place} flowered in the snow,
  ($e.what=stone) A stone fell out of the sky at {$e.place},
  A wonder was seen at {$e.place} in {$e.season},
ann.sg.wnd.b
  and the old ones said it meant {ann.goodsign}, and the young ones {ann.badsign},
  and everyone went to see it with {food} in a cloth, and came home quiet,
  and nobody knew, and the {ann.craftfolk} still argue about it,

song.games
  {ann.sg.gm.a}\n{ann.sg.gm.b}\n{song.refrain}
ann.sg.gm.a
  (has:$e.a) Who won at {$e.place}? {$e.a:name} won,
  (has:$e.a) {$e.a:name} of {$e.a.home}, faster than the wind,
  At the games at {$e.place} in {$e.season},
ann.sg.gm.b
  and the {colour.holy} ribbon was tied on the winner's arm,
  and the losers drank {drink}, and the winners drank more,
  and the {ann.instrument.or.drum} went all night,
ann.instrument.or.drum
  drum
  pipes

song.law
  The law came down from {$seat} in {$e.season},\n{ann.sg.law.b}\n{song.refrain}
ann.sg.law.b
  and we read it, and we laughed, and we paid in {crop},
  ($e.what=tax) and the tax took the {crop} out of the children's mouths,
  and it said we must, and we swore {oath} we would, and we did not,

song.trial
  {ann.sg.tr.a}\n{ann.sg.tr.b}\n{song.refrain}
ann.sg.tr.a
  (has:$e.a) They took {$e.a:name} to the judges at {$e.place},
  (has:$e.a) {$e.a:name} stood up in the court and would not bow,
  There was a trial at {$e.place} in {$e.season},
ann.sg.tr.b
  ($e.verdict=acquitted) and the judges let {$e.a:obj} go, and the town cheered,
  ($e.verdict=condemned) and they hanged {$e.a:obj} at the crossroads, and the town was quiet,
  ($e.verdict=exiled) and they sent {$e.a:obj} over {mountain} and nobody followed,
  ($e.verdict=fined) and the fine was more than a {beast} is worth,
  (!has:$e.a) and whoever it was, they hanged them,

song.embassy
  The envoys came to {$e.place} with gifts,\n{ann.sg.emb.b}\n{song.refrain}
ann.sg.emb.b
  and they talked all day, and they ate our {food} all night,
  and nobody knew what was agreed, and the {herd} did not care,

song.accident
  {ann.sg.acc.a}\n{ann.sg.acc.b}\n{song.refrain}
ann.sg.acc.a
  ($e.what=mine) Down in the mine at {$e.place} the roof came in,
  ($e.what=ship) The ship went out from {$e.place} and did not come in,
  ($e.what=bridge) The bridge at {$e.place} went into the river,
  ($e.what=train) The train came off the line near {$e.place},
  There was a disaster at {$e.place} in {$e.season},
ann.sg.acc.b
  ($e.value>0) and {#$e.value:about} did not come home that night,
  and the women stood at the gate in {colour.mourn} till morning,
  and the ones who built it of {material} said it was nobody's fault,

song.price
  ($e.out=1) Bread is dear, bread is dear, and the children are thin,\n{ann.sg.pr.b}\n{song.refrain}
  ($e.out=0) There is {crop} enough this year and the cup is full,\n{ann.sg.pr.b}\n{song.refrain}
ann.sg.pr.b
  and the traders count their {ann.coin.or.shells} in the back room,
  and we sing over the empty {vessel} because we cannot do anything else,
ann.coin.or.shells
  (age>=medieval) {coin}
  shells

song.beasts
  ($e.what=none) The {game} did not come down to the river this year,\n{ann.sg.bs.b}\n{song.refrain}
  ($e.what=many) The {game} came down so many the ground was brown with them,\n{ann.sg.bs.b}\n{song.refrain}
  ($e.what=great) We brought down a great {game.one} at {$e.place},\n{ann.sg.bs.b}\n{song.refrain}
  ($e.what=killed) The {game.one} turned at {$e.place} and killed the hunters,\n{ann.sg.bs.b}\n{song.refrain}
  ($e.what=late|$e.what=early) The {game} came when nobody was ready,\n{ann.sg.bs.b}\n{song.refrain}
ann.sg.bs.b
  and we sang to them the old songs, with {instrument}, and they did not listen,
  and the {fuel} fires were high that night, or low,

song.show
  There was something new at {$e.place} in {$e.season},\n{ann.sg.sh.b}\n{song.refrain}
ann.sg.sh.b
  (has:$e.a) and {$e.a:name} made it, and half the town walked out,
  and nobody liked it, and everybody went in their best {garment.n},

song.visit
  {$e.a:full} came to {$e.place} in {$e.season},\n{ann.sg.vs.b}\n{song.refrain}
ann.sg.vs.b
  and we swept the street and hid the good {drink},
  and {$e.a:name} ate our {food} and went away,
)VG"
